From 17dfa233606db228d5c3e3b3ac981e43c64f6cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolas Joshua Britton <joshua@exabit.io>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:25:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?spec:=20adaptive=20MTP=20draft=20depth=20(draft?=
 =?UTF-8?q?-mtp-adaptive)=20=E2=80=94=20upstream=20PR=20#27210=20by=20stew?=
 =?UTF-8?q?675,=20applied=20on=20the=20fork's=20speculative=20code?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream PR https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27210 (head d236d41a2, 2026-09-08):
--spec-type draft-mtp-adaptive with --spec-draft-n-max as the ceiling and
--spec-draft-n-min-adaptive (default 3) as the floor; a climb counter and a
weighted drop-pressure accumulator move the depth per sequence. The author's
numbers on Qwen3.8-27B Q8_0 (2x R9700, tensor split): reasoning 1.71x, prose
1.88x, code 2.60x (fixed depth 3: 2.31x), recall 4.9x over no drafting.

Merge notes: common/speculative.{h,cpp} conflicted with the fork's
common_speculative_reset / deferred-prefill state next to the PR's
accept_partial and adaptive members; both kept, the PR's constructor
signature taken. The PR's delta-net-base.cpp conv-state hunk (t_min loop
bound) is NOT applied: milpster's fork found it costs 38% of prompt
processing with MTP on a layer split (PR27210-ADAPTIVE-MTP-2026-08-25.md)
and it is unrelated to the feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
